## 2026-11-25 - OWL-RL license correction (W3C-20150513)

Context:
Legal review of the bundled third-party licenses found that the owlrl license
file did not match the license declared by the library. The file in
`licenses/python/owlrl-LICENSE.txt` was an inaccurate transcription of the
W3C Software Notice and Document License (2015-05-13), SPDX `W3C-20150513`.
The locked owlrl version (7.1.4) ships the verbatim text. The `owlrl`
lower bound `>=7.0.0` also referenced a version that does not exist on PyPI
(the lowest 7.x release is 7.1.1).

Changes:
1. licenses/python/owlrl-LICENSE.txt: replaced with the verbatim `LICENSE.txt`
   shipped in the owlrl 7.1.4 wheel (W3C-20150513).
2. licenses/README.md: OWL-RL row now states the minimum version `>=7.1.1` and
   the SPDX identifier `W3C-20150513`; the license summary table is updated
   accordingly (previously "W3C Software License").
3. pyproject.toml: `owlrl>=7.0.0` -> `owlrl>=7.1.1` (no behavioural change,
   since 7.0.0 is not published and the resolver already picked 7.1.x).
4. uv.lock: only the root `requires-dist` specifier for owlrl updated to
   `>=7.1.1`. No package version or hash changed. The lock was edited by hand
   because `uv lock` in this environment rewrites every registry URL to the
   internal proxy (`UV_INDEX_URL`), which must not be committed.

Modified files:
- licenses/python/owlrl-LICENSE.txt
- licenses/README.md
- pyproject.toml
- uv.lock
- changelogs/v0.10.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-11-25.log

Test result:
Full suite: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"
-> 11473 passed, 334 skipped, 8 deselected, 0 failed.
Note: `uv lock --check` reports the lock as stale on HEAD too in this
environment (proxy index), so it is not a usable signal here.

## Genie Pages (UC Knowledge Pages) read on-behalf-of the signed-in user

Context: Context → Pages (Genie Pages) listed and previewed UC Knowledge Pages
with the app service principal. In Databricks Apps the page list and bodies
must follow the caller's Unity Catalog permissions, like the other OBO data
reads (v0.9.0). Local / PAT mode is unchanged.

Changes:
1. src/api/routers/internal/domain.py: `_knowledge_page_service` now uses
   `get_data_plane_client` (OBO, fail-closed) instead of `get_databricks_client`.
   `list_knowledge_pages` and `preview_knowledge_page` re-raise
   `AuthorizationError` instead of wrapping it as `InfrastructureError`.
2. src/back/core/databricks/KnowledgePageService.py: 401/403 hint texts no longer
   reference the app identity (they now refer to the user's token / identity).
3. tests/units/api/test_knowledge_pages_route.py: +3 tests (OBO client used, no SP
   fallback; `AuthorizationError` surfaces unchanged on list and preview).
4. docs/deployment.md, docs/user-guide.md: OBO scope now lists Knowledge Pages
   list / preview.

Not changed (follow-up): ontology generation (`GenerateWorkflow.load_knowledge_page_bodies`)
still reads page bodies with the service principal. Its detection runs in a plain
`threading.Thread` (`ontology.py`) that does not carry the request identity, so it
needs the user token passed explicitly.

Open risk: the Knowledge Pages REST API may require a user-token scope beyond
`sql` (`user_api_scopes`). Not verifiable offline; verify after deploy. A 403 on
Pages after deploy points to a missing scope. Identity scopes must not be added.

Modified files:
- src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
- src/back/core/databricks/KnowledgePageService.py
- tests/units/api/test_knowledge_pages_route.py
- docs/deployment.md
- docs/user-guide.md
- changelogs/v0.10.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-11-25.log

Test result:
Full suite: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"
-> 11476 passed, 334 skipped, 8 deselected, 0 failed.
